        "text": "**Developing Correlated Logs**\n\nI've just finished the `write_correlated_logs.py` file. It's set up to import `google.cloud.logging` for identification purposes and uses a `cloud_logging.Client`. The core is the `write_correlated_log_events` function, which implements the logging logic.\n\n\n**Implementing Logging Solution**\n\nI've completed the `write_correlated_logs.py` file, incorporating `google.cloud.logging` for identification and a `cloud_logging.Client`. The core `write_correlated_log_events` function handles logging with optional correlation IDs, generating new ones via `uuid.uuid4()` when needed. Logs include `correlation_id` in `jsonPayload`. A Python logging fallback and example usage are implemented for demonstration.\n\n\n",
